entation gate rather than merely stale. The reviewed head could not have passed its own gate whatever verdict it received. It now names db34afe2, the live artifact at cmd/gitseq-mcp, which is the path whose behaviour it describes. That will be superseded when this merges and the page will flare then; that is the signal working, not a defect.\n\nThe known-failing citation baseline loses this page from three entries, because it no longer names the whole-repository artifact 15390758 or the comma-joined d314fadc and dd237f34. I edited those three lines by hand rather than regenerating the file, because regeneration reads the live workroom and would have swept in unrelated movement from your acts and mine. The three citations stay recorded for the other pages that still name them.\n\nI also carried current main, which conflicted in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main_test.go. Both sides were additive, appending tests at the same place, and the resolution keeps both families; both pass. The judgement from 06e211c2 stands unchanged and is the thing most worth your eye: this call site does not use residentclient.UndefinedKindWarning, because it needs a snapshot anyway for the notes and a snapshot can be a cold fold, so calling the shared helper would fold twice per act. That leaves main's convergence one call short here.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet, go build, full go test ./... green, uncached internal/docset green at 80s, go test -race ./cmd/gitseq-mcp green, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, merges into main cleanly.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:94cdae6741d8dddf8e50e3aafb35a2b16a15c7a6","conditions":"Report approved or changes-requested for exact head bff7dd1170bb679b6a8fd98231c5a5c8948f3729, naming artifact 94cdae67 for cmd/gitseq-mcp; do not merge.","head":"bff7dd1170bb679b6a8fd98231c5a5c8948f3729","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}